  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"schemabench_0150\" consists of 15 tables. The primary purpose of this schema is to manage various aspects of a social media platform, including user moderation, tagging, saving stories, voting, invitations, messaging, moderation logs, internal metadata, schema migrations, story management, hidden stories, user management, and commenting.\nThe \"moderations\" table represents user moderation actions. It contains columns for the moderation id, the user id, the story id, the comment id, the reason for the action, the suggested action, and the creation timestamp. The story_id, user_id, and comment_id are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"stories\", \"users\", and \"comments\" tables.\nThe \"tags\" table contains information about tags, including the tag id, tag name, description, and creation and update timestamps.\nThe \"story_tags\" table serves as a junction table for many-to-many relationships between stories and tags. It contains story id and tag id as primary keys, and both are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"tags\" and \"stories\" tables.\nThe \"saved_stories\" table maintains a record of which users have saved which stories. It contains user id and story id as primary keys, and both are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"users\" and \"stories\" tables.\nThe \"domains\" table contains information about domains, including the domain id, domain name, and creation and update timestamps.\nThe \"votes\" table records user votes on stories and comments. It contains user id, story id, comment id, vote value, and vote timestamp. The story_id, user_id, and comment_id are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"stories\", \"users\", and \"comments\" tables.\nThe \"invitations\" table keeps track of user invitations. It contains invitation id, user id, email, and creation timestamp. The user_id is a foreign key referencing the id in the \"users\" table.\nThe \"messages\" table stores user messages. It contains message id, sender id, recipient id, subject, body, creation and read timestamps, and flags for whether the message was deleted by the sender or recipient. The recipient_id and sender_id are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"users\" table.\nThe \"moderation_logs\" table logs actions taken on stories. It contains log id, story id, user id, action, and creation timestamp. The story_id and user_id are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"stories\" and \"users\" tables.\nThe \"ar_internal_metadata\" table stores metadata about the Rails application's internal state. It contains key-value pairs and timestamps.\nThe \"schema_migrations\" table keeps track of which schema migrations have been run.\nThe \"stories\" table manages user stories. It contains story id, user id, title, description, URL, creation and update timestamps, moderation status, and score. The user_id is a foreign key referencing the id in the \"users\" table.\nThe \"hidden_stories\" table keeps track of which users have hidden which stories. It contains user id and story id as primary keys, and both are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"users\" and \"stories\" tables.\nThe \"users\" table manages user accounts. It contains user id, username, email, encrypted password, password digest, creation and update timestamps, settings, and ban status.\nThe \"comments\" table manages user comments. It contains comment id, story id, user id, body, creation and update timestamps. The story_id and user_id are foreign keys referencing the respective ids in the \"stories\" and \"users\" tables.\nThis schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing foreign key constraints. For instance, the story_id in the \"moderations\" table references the id in the \"stories\" table, ensuring that all story_ids in the \"moderations\" table correspond to valid story ids in the \"stories\" table. Similarly, the user_id in the \"moderations\" table references the id in the \"users\" table, ensuring that all user_ids in the \"moderations\" table correspond to valid user ids in the \"users\" table.\nThe schema is designed to be flexible and scalable, with tables representing different aspects of the platform and relationships between them. It allows for easy management of user moderation, tagging, saving, voting, invitations, messaging, and more.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project involves the development of a technology-focused community platform for link aggregation and discussion, similar to Hacker News. The platform, named Lobsters, is designed to cater primarily to enthusiasts and professionals in technology, programming, and computer science. It operates with an invite-only model to ensure high-quality content and discourse.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To provide a platform for sharing and discussing links related to technology, programming, and computer science.\n- To maintain a high standard of content quality through an invite-only membership system.\n- To enhance community transparency with a public moderation log.\n- To facilitate community replication by operating as open-source software.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Community Members: Users who submit links and participate in discussions.\n- Moderators: Users responsible for content moderation and maintaining community standards.\n- Administrators: Users with elevated privileges to manage platform operations.\n- Visitors: Non-members who can view content but not participate.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- User Registration and Management: Support for invite-based user registration and profile management.\n- Content Submission: Users can submit links to articles, research papers, and blog posts.\n- Discussion Threads: Users can engage in threaded discussions related to submitted content.\n- Voting System: Users can vote on stories and comments to influence content visibility.\n- Tagging System: Stories can be tagged for improved categorization and searchability.\n- Story Moderation: Tools for moderators to manage content quality, including moderation logs.\n- Messaging System: Direct messaging capabilities for communication between members.\n- Story and Comment Management: Functions for saving, hiding, and moderating stories and comments.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: The platform should efficiently support growth in user base and content volume.\n- Security: Implementation of robust security measures, including encrypted passwords and data protection.\n- Performance: Ensuring low latency for user interactions, even with increased load.\n- Transparency: Access to public moderation logs to uphold community standards.\n- Usability: Intuitive user interface and navigation to promote ease of use.\n- Open-Source Accessibility: Available for other communities to replicate and adapt.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0150.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0150\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `encrypted_password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password_digest` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `settings` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `ban_status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `stories` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `moderation_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `moderations` (\n  `moderation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reason` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `suggested_action` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`moderation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `moderations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderations_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tags` (\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `tag_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`tag_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `story_tags` (\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tag_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`story_id`, `tag_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `story_tags_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `story_tags_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`tag_id`) REFERENCES `tags` (`tag_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `saved_stories` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `saved_stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `saved_stories_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `domains` (\n  `domain_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `domain_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`domain_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `votes` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `vote_value` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vote_timestamp` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `story_id`, `comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `votes_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `comments` (`comment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `invitations` (\n  `invitation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`invitation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `invitations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `messages` (\n  `message_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recipient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subject` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `read_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_by_sender` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `deleted_by_recipient` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`message_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `messages_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recipient_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `moderation_logs` (\n  `log_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `action` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`log_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `moderation_logs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `moderation_logs_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hidden_stories` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `story_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `story_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `hidden_stories_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `hidden_stories_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`story_id`) REFERENCES `stories` (`story_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `ar_internal_metadata` (\n  `key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `value` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`key`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `schema_migrations` (\n  `version` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`version`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
